Design Summary

R2 and R3 use OSPF process 1 to provide dynamic routing across the 10.23.23.0/30 Area 0 transit network.

R2 uses 2.2.2.2 as its OSPF router ID, while R3 uses 3.3.3.3.

R3 is designed as the ABR connecting Area 0 and Area 10. The design demonstrates inter-area routing, area summarization, OSPF LSAs, stub area types, NSSA, passive interfaces, authentication, and default route injection.

R2 also participates in EIGRP AS 100 and serves as the redistribution boundary between the EIGRP and OSPF routing domains.

The OSPF design provides dynamic routing between the enterprise network segments while demonstrating multiple OSPF control-plane and route-optimization features.
